The way the standard function obtains the value to pass is specific to
the client, which is why @sysname{} does not impose a particular
technique.  One possibility for client code is to define the standard
function as a @emph{closure}, closing over the @code{client} object.
Another possibility is to keep the @code{client} object as the value of
a special variable.
